  "body": "As someone who has been quite happy with how the chrome.serial API worked up until deprecation, I am wondering why this spec uses streams for communication (which seem to be in flux/not final?) while ArrayBuffers - used by chrome.serial - are easy to deal with and widely understood/supported.  Maybe I am missing something?\n\nref:\n\nhttps://developer.chrome.com/apps/serial#method-send\nhttps://developer.chrome.com/apps/serial#event-onReceive\n",
